  "notes": [
    "Reflexive counterpart of **morir**; same stem changes: o→ue in presente/subjuntivo (except nosotros), o→u in the 3rd-person pretérito (se murió, se murieron)",
    "Imperfecto and future/conditional are regular, with no stem change",
    "Irregular past participle: **muerto** (used in the compound tenses: se ha muerto)",
    "**Morirse** emphasizes the personal experience/process of dying, or is used figuratively, more than plain **morir**",
    "Common usage: *morirse de hambre* (to be starving), *morirse de risa* (to die laughing), *morirse de ganas de algo* (to be dying to do something)"
  ],
